{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Context\n\nDiscovered while fixing 79d6 (financial-maroon-toucan, Gerrit 1658), which unguarded the\nregion env so every live-LLM matrix arm resolves a Bedrock region.\n\n`tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py` sets\n`_live_llm_ready = _live_llm.live_llm_ready()` — a probe that answers \"is the credential\npresent for the provider THIS ARM resolves from the standard model class\". But the module\nbypasses model-class resolution and pins `_MODEL = \"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\"`.\nOn the anthropic and openai arms the probe says READY (an Anthropic/OpenAI key exists) while\nevery cell actually calls Bedrock — an arm that carries no AWS credential, because the OIDC\nstep is gated `if: matrix.provider == 'bedrock'`.\n\nA module's readiness sentinel must agree with the model it pins. Here it cannot.\n\nIt is the ONLY bedrock-pinned module in the `llm_live` lane: `test_bedrock_cache_live.py` is\nalso bedrock-pinned but carries no `_live_llm_ready` sentinel (plain `external` + its own\n`REBAR_LIVE_BEDROCK` opt-in), so it runs in the complement job and is unaffected.\n\n# Disposition — option (b) is REJECTED; do not re-litigate\n\n**Un-gating the OIDC step to all arms is rejected**: it hands AWS credentials to arms holding\nthird-party API keys (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` / `OPENAI_API_KEY`), widening the blast radius of the\nscoped Bedrock CI role for ZERO coverage gain — it would call the same model from three arms\nand learn the same fact three times. The OIDC step stays gated to `matrix.provider == 'bedrock'`.\n\nAlso rejected: un-pinning `_MODEL` so the eval follows each arm. The pin exists to hold the\nmodel fixed while reproducing bug 0707; unpinning turns a single-model regression reproduction\ninto a 3x-spend cross-provider eval, which is a different test with a different purpose.\n\n**Approved: option (a) — a provider-aware readiness sentinel.** Test-harness correctness with\nzero credential-surface change.\n\n# Plan\n\n1. `tests/external/_live_llm.py`: give `live_llm_ready()` an optional `required_provider`\n   argument. When supplied, readiness additionally requires the arm's `configured_provider()`\n   to MATCH it, so a module that pins a provider is ready only on the arm that runs it.\n   Add a `skip_unless_provider(provider)` mark factory whose reason names the mismatch\n   (module pins X, arm resolves Y) so the skip is VISIBLE, not silent. Purely additive:\n   the no-argument call and the module-level `skip_without_live_llm` are unchanged, so the\n   seven modules that do not pin a provider keep their exact current behaviour.\n2. `tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py`: pass the pinned provider to the\n   sentinel and apply `skip_unless_provider(\"bedrock\")` on both tests.\n3. Regression test for the invariant.\n\nCanary-safe: the all-skip canary fires only when collected>=1 and executed==0. On a non-bedrock\narm the other `llm_live` modules still execute, so the arm stays green for the right reason.\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — A module that pins a provider is `_live_llm_ready` only on the arm that resolves\n  that provider; on other arms it skips with a reason naming both the pinned provider and the\n  arm's resolved provider.\n- [ ] AC2 — `tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py` uses that gate for\n  `bedrock`, and modules that pin nothing are behaviourally unchanged.\n- [ ] AC3 — A test pins the invariant (a pinned-provider module is not ready on a mismatched\n  arm, and is ready on the matching arm when its credential is present), and the rejection of\n  option (b) is recorded on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786571675425672001,"uuid":"6e544522-da4a-49a3-8348-9e78ff309f99"}